WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.839 --> 00:00:06.799
In this video you'll invite many teachers at once with a spreadsheet file, called a C-S-V.

2
00:00:07.301 --> 00:00:15.261
Open Invitations from the menu. You'll find the template button here at the top of the page, and a Bulk Invite button next to it.

3
00:00:15.762 --> 00:00:25.562
Start by downloading the template. It's an empty file with the right column names already in it. Open it in your spreadsheet app and add one teacher on each row.

4
00:00:26.063 --> 00:00:48.973
The columns are email, first name, last name, grade level, role, department, and subject area. Email, first name, last name, and grade level are required on every row, and any row missing a name is skipped. For grade level, use E-S, M-S, H-S, or H-E, and put a semicolon between two or more.

5
00:00:49.474 --> 00:01:02.344
Keep each value free of commas, because a comma inside a cell splits it in two when the file is read. You can invite up to two hundred teachers in one upload. If you have more, split them into two files.

6
00:01:02.846 --> 00:01:08.286
When you're done, save the file as a C-S-V. Then select Bulk Invite.

7
00:01:08.788 --> 00:01:12.868
Drag the file into the box, or select the box to browse for it.

8
00:01:13.368 --> 00:01:25.238
A line appears telling you how many emails are ready to invite, and how many rows were skipped because a first or last name was missing. Here, one row has no last name, so it won't be sent.

9
00:01:25.739 --> 00:01:35.469
Select Send Invitations. When it finishes, you'll see a summary of how many were sent, how many were skipped, and how many couldn't be sent, with the reasons.

10
00:01:35.971 --> 00:01:45.761
Skipped means the person was already invited, or already has a seat at your school. That's not a problem. Here, Alex Kim already had an invitation waiting.

11
00:01:46.262 --> 00:01:54.202
Close the window and the new invitations are in your list right away. Each teacher gets the same email as in a single invitation.

12
00:01:54.702 --> 00:01:58.792
To keep track of them, see the video on managing invitations.
